# The rules of hien_lts.obj -- Hindi, hand-written.
#
# Everything else in this tree came out of IBM's objects through
# tools/delta-notation.py. This file did not: it is the first rule in the
# project written by a person rather than lifted, and it is written in the
# same notation for the same reason the lifted files are -- one operation to
# a line, the machine's own registers and argument stack, nothing carried by
# indentation. docs/building.md says what each verb means.
#
# `from hien_lts.obj' names an object that does not exist. The emitter reads
# the name only to group the constants a rule addresses by symbol, and this
# rule addresses none, so nothing looks for the file. That is deliberate: a
# new symbol would go into the language's shared symbol pool and move every
# address after it, which lang/hien/rules/symbols records by position.
#
# What it does: puts two numbers into the language's global variables before
# anything is spoken, standing where enus writes them inline. Devanagari is
# written without case, so the machine's letter-case variable is of no use and
# is left at nought.
#
# What it does NOT do, and this is worth saying plainly rather than leaving to
# be discovered: neither number changes what comes out. 4130 gets 1, which is
# what enus writes there too, and 4134 gets 3 where enus writes 2 -- and
# nothing in any of the nine languages' rules ever reads 4134. Grep it. So
# this rule is structural: it proves that a rule written by a person lifts,
# links, is reached from e_vars and runs, and it is where Hindi's globals will
# go. It is not yet why Hindi sounds different from English. That is entirely
# the four duration numbers in es_val.dr, and it was measured rather than
# assumed -- put those four back to English's values and the two languages
# speak byte-identical samples with this rule still in place.
#
# 4130 next door does have a reader, insert_dict_root in et_morph.dr, which is
# where a Hindi value that reaches something would start.

rule hi_lang_globals from hien_lts.obj
shape frame 196 argbase 8 params 1
label L0 was _hi_lang_globals
  alu andl imm 0 slot -4
  load movl slotaddr -104 into r0
  push imm 0
  push slotaddr -104
  call setjmp3 arity 2 depth 2
  cmp testl reg r0 reg r0
  load movl state 0 into r6
  popreg r1
  popreg r1
  branch jne to L1
  load movl slotaddr -104 into r0
  push slotaddr -104
  load movl slotaddr -40 into r0
  push slotaddr -40
  load movl slotaddr -28 into r0
  push slotaddr -28
  load movl slotaddr -16 into r0
  push slotaddr -16
  load movl slotaddr -196 into r0
  push slotaddr -196
  push state 0
  call ventproc arity 6 depth 6
  popn 6
  cmp testl reg r0 reg r0
  branch je to L2
label L1 was at_fail
  push imm 94
  push reg r6
  call vretproc arity 2 depth 2
  popreg r1
  popreg r1
  load movl imm 94 into r0
  jump to L3
label L2 was at_body
  push reg r6
  call ZZfence_null arity 1 depth 1
  push reg r6
  store movw imm 1 ind reg r6 4130
  store movw imm 3 ind reg r6 4134
  call succeed arity 1 depth 2
  popreg r1
  popreg r1
  load movl imm 0 into r0
label L3 was at_done
  return reg r0
end
